---
description: Next.js / design system rules. The tokens are fixed.
globs: ["web/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Design tokens (SPEC §5.11) are **fixed**. Adding a one-off value is a rejected change.

- Colors, exactly five plus three semantic: `--void #000000`, `--panel #0B0B0C`,
  `--rule #1C1C1E`, `--text #EDEDED`, `--muted #6E6E73`; `--capital #4C8DFF` (what you own),
  `--risk #E8A33D` (what you are exposed to), `--alert #FF3B30` (hard flags only).
  No other hex values anywhere. No gradients.
- Zero border-radius. Zero box-shadow. Panels are separated by 1px `--rule` hairlines,
  never by cards.
- All numerals in a monospace face with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`. This is an
  instrument readout; digits align.
- Five type steps, no sixth. Labels are uppercase, tracked, `--muted`. Values are large,
  monospace, `--text`.
- 8px vertical rhythm. Single column, max-width ~880px.
- Motion: one load sequence where numerals count up once, then stop. Nothing else animates.
  Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- No component library, no third-party font CDN (self-host), no analytics, no telemetry.
- **No currency anywhere.** No `$`, no currency formatting, no field named value/balance/
  amount. The frontend receives weights only.
- Copy: active voice, sentence case, plain verbs. Errors say what happened and what to do,
  and never apologise. Empty state is an invitation to act.
- Quality floor, unannounced: responsive to 375px, visible keyboard focus, real contrast.
